<title>SINGAPORE: Acer raises investment in Japan unit.</title>
<headline>Acer raises investment in Japan unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Acer Computer International (ACI) said on Tuesday it had increased its investment in Acer Japan Corporation (AJC) by about US$4.4 million (509 million yen).</p>
<p>It said in a statement it had subscribed for 10,180 new shares at par.</p>
<p>The new investment brings AJC's paid-up capital to 1.14 billion yen with ACI's investment at 1.14 billion yen.</p>
<p>ACI now holds 99.9 percent of AJC, up from 99.8 percent.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newroom( 65-8703080)</p>
</text>
